            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of headache: a dentigerous cyst in the maxillary sinus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1174-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a patient with a dentigerous cyst in the maxillary sinus presenting as two months of intermittent, unilateral, pressure-like headaches. The diagnosis was suspected after an upright Waters' projection radiogram and confirmed histologically after surgical removal. The patient was symptom free one year later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
